; Format: scl blocks (Scala .scl scales, one per [slot])
; =====================================================================================
;  Wakes — SCALES
; =====================================================================================
;
;  The scales MARBLES' X quantizer (•• + FFWD / RWD on the X page) and PLAITS' FREQUENCY
;  quantizer (SETTINGS T2 / T3) choose from. Both modules use this one list.
;
;  Wakes reads and applies this .cnfg file every time it turns ON.
;
;  Lines starting with ; or # are comments. Delete this file to get the default back:
;  Wakes writes it again at the next ON.
;
; ---- slots ----
;  There are 7 scale slots, [1] to [7]. A slot that is not in this file is empty, and the
;  scale buttons skip it. A slot above [7] is dropped (the log says the file is overloaded).
;  Every slot has its own glyph, so slot 2 always flashes ●●○○ whatever scale is in it.
;  Presets (PRST) remember the scale SLOT: change what is in a slot and a preset that used it
;  plays the new scale.
;
; ---- a scale ----
;  Under its numbered [slot], a scale is written in the Scala format (.scl), the format of
;  the Scala scale archive and of Scale Workshop (https://sevish.com/scaleworkshop/): build
;  a scale there, export it as a Scala file (.scl), open that in a text editor and paste it
;  under a numbered [slot] section here.
;
;  .scl format:
;    lines starting with '!' are Scala-format comments
;    the first other line is the scale's NAME (it can be empty)
;    the next line is how many PITCHES comprise the scale
;    then, one pitch designation appears per line, the last one defining the period/octave.
;
;  In .scl format, the root (1/1, 0 cents) is not written: every scale starts on the root.
;  Where that root sits:
;    MARBLES' X: at 0 V. Routed to V/Oct, X is added to FREQUENCY, so the root is
;      wherever FREQUENCY is set.
;    PLAITS' quantizer: on C, or on the note you tune by ear (see tune_by_ear below).
;  Pitches can be defined in CENTS or as RATIOS of the root. A pitch definition containing
;  a "." is in CENTS (100.0 is a semitone); without one it is a RATIO (3/2, or 2 for 2/1).
;  Write them in any order; each one must be above the root and below the period. Wakes
;  takes 64 pitches at most, with the period included: enough for 31-EDO or 53-EDO.
;
; ---- Wakes' extras (other Scala programs ignore these) ----
;
;  You can define scales pretty simply using ratios and cents, but Wakes offers Mutable
;  Instruments-derived features that let you play around with those scales.
;
;  Note weight: a whole number 0-255 after a pitch defines its weight.
;    Weights are how Marbles' STEPS fader thins the scale out as it moves from its centre
;    to 100%. Just past the centre every degree of the scale is in: a scale written on all
;    12 semitones, like Marbles' major below, is chromatic there. Turning STEPS further up
;    drops the low-weight notes first, leaving the notes that define the scale, then fewer,
;    until only the root (always 255) remains. Below the centre STEPS does not quantize at
;    all: X glides smoothly between values. A pitch without a weight gets 255 (it is always
;    there). Any other text left in after a note's pitch definition is ignored.
;    Important: Without note weights, Marbles cannot play around with which notes are 
;    available on the scale. As you define scales, remember which intervals sound good, and
;    weight them to your taste.
;
;  plaits = N (written above the scale's name, under its [slot]): PLAITS' quantizer plays
;    the degrees with a weight of N or more. 0 (or leaving it out) = every degree.
;    Marbles' scales below use 32 (pelog: 0). In the major scale, this makes Plaits'
;    quantizer select the 7 notes of the major scale, not all 12 of its scale degrees,
;    which would just be the chromatic scale.
;    It helps to understand that, for example, if you wanted to use diatonic scales (musical
;    modes), you would start with the chromatic definition Scala block (100.0, 200.0, etc.),
;    and then set plaits = 32 and use the note weights to bring out the 7 actual intervals
;    of the diatonic scale you are trying to create. The seven modes at the end of this
;    file are written exactly that way.
;
;  tune_by_ear = on / off (written above the scale's name, under its [slot]): Tune By Ear,
;    for PLAITS' quantizer. On (or leaving it out): tune FREQUENCY by ear with the quantizer
;    off (TRIG to listen), then turn the quantizer on (SETTINGS T3): the note FREQUENCY was
;    playing becomes the scale's root, between semitones too. Stepping to another scale
;    keeps that root; turning the quantizer off and on again takes a new one. Off: the
;    scale stays on C, for scales whose notes belong to fixed pitches. Presets load their
;    scale on C.
;
; ---- if something is wrong ----
;  The log (WAKES/LOGS/) names every line Wakes cannot read. If ANY scale in this file has a
;  problem, Wakes ignores the file and uses the default scales instead.
;  Turn on "scales" in logs.cnfg to see which scales were loaded at every ON.
;
;  Wakes' default scales.cnfg ships with slots [1]-[6] containing the original scales curated
;  for Mutable Instruments' Marbles (marbles/settings.cc, Emilie Gillet, MIT),
;  rewritten as Scala. Note names in the comments assume the root is C.

[1]
plaits = 32
tune_by_ear = on
! Marbles' major scale. Note names assume a root of C.
major
12
!
 100.0   16    ; C#  (root C)
 200.0   96    ; D   (root C)
 300.0   24    ; D#  (root C)
 400.0  128    ; E   (root C)
 500.0   64    ; F   (root C)
 600.0    8    ; F#  (root C)
 700.0  192    ; G   (root C)
 800.0   16    ; G#  (root C)
 900.0   96    ; A   (root C)
1000.0   24    ; A#  (root C)
1100.0  128    ; B   (root C)
2/1

[2]
plaits = 32
tune_by_ear = on
! Marbles' minor scale. Note names assume a root of C.
minor
12
!
 100.0   16    ; C#  (root C)
 200.0   96    ; D   (root C)
 300.0  128    ; Eb  (root C)
 400.0    8    ; E   (root C)
 500.0   64    ; F   (root C)
 600.0    4    ; F#  (root C)
 700.0  192    ; G   (root C)
 800.0   96    ; G#  (root C)
 900.0   16    ; A   (root C)
1000.0  128    ; Bb  (root C)
1100.0   16    ; B   (root C)
2/1

[3]
plaits = 32
tune_by_ear = on
! Marbles' pentatonic scale. Note names assume a root of C.
pentatonic
12
!
 100.0    4    ; C#  (root C)
 200.0   96    ; D   (root C)
 300.0    4    ; Eb  (root C)
 400.0    4    ; E   (root C)
 500.0  140    ; F   (root C)
 600.0    4    ; F#  (root C)
 700.0  192    ; G   (root C)
 800.0    4    ; G#  (root C)
 900.0   96    ; A   (root C)
1000.0    4    ; Bb  (root C)
1100.0    4    ; B   (root C)
2/1

[4]
plaits = 0
tune_by_ear = off
! Pelog: seven degrees, all of them the scale. Note names assume a root of C
! (+ / - = a little sharp / flat of that note).
pelog
7
!
 153.0  128    ; Db+ (root C)
 315.0   32    ; Eb- (root C)
 552.0    8    ; F#- (root C)
 705.96 192    ; G   (root C)
 848.04  64    ; Ab  (root C)
1058.04  16    ; Bb+ (root C)
2/1

[5]
plaits = 32
tune_by_ear = off
! Raag Bhairav That, just intonation. Swara names, relative to Sa (the root).
bhairav
12
!
256/243 128    ; Komal Re
9/8       4    ; Re
6/5       4    ; Komal Ga
5/4     128    ; Ga
4/3      64    ; Ma
45/32     4    ; Tivre Ma
3/2     192    ; Pa
128/81   64    ; Komal Dha
27/16     4    ; Dha
9/5       4    ; Komal Ni
15/8     64    ; Ni
2/1

[6]
plaits = 32
tune_by_ear = off
! Raag Shri, just intonation. Swara names, relative to Sa (the root).
shri
12
!
256/243   4    ; Komal Re
9/8     128    ; Re
6/5      64    ; Komal Ga
5/4       4    ; Ga
4/3     128    ; Ma
45/32     4    ; Tivre Ma
3/2     192    ; Pa
128/81    4    ; Komal Dha
27/16    64    ; Dha
9/5     128    ; Komal Ni
15/8      4    ; Ni
2/1

; [7] is empty: yours. For example, remove the ; from these lines for a whole-tone scale:
; [7]
; ! six equal steps, every one always there
; whole-tone
; 6
; 200.0
; 400.0
; 600.0
; 800.0
; 1000.0
; 2/1

; =====================================================================================
;  THE SEVEN MODES (diatonic scales), ready to copy
; =====================================================================================
;
;  To use one: copy its lines, from "; plaits = 32" down to "; 2/1", into this file under a
;  [slot] line of your choice (a free slot, or one you are replacing), and remove the "; "
;  at the start of each of those lines. Leave the "; ----" title line out.
;
;  Each mode is cut out of the chromatic scale with weights, the way Marbles' major scale
;  is (Ionian below IS Marbles' major, note for note):
;    the mode's notes     root 255, 5th 192, 3rd 128, 7th 128, 2nd 96, 6th 96, 4th 64
;    the other 5 notes    the 3rd or 7th the mode does NOT use 24, the tritone 8, others 16
;  So STEPS keeps the root, fifth, third and seventh longest, and plaits = 32 gives Plaits
;  the mode's 7 notes. In Locrian the 5th is the diminished fifth, its defining note, so
;  it takes the 5th's weight. Note names assume a root of C; with tune_by_ear on, each
;  mode starts on whatever note you tune Plaits to.
;
; ---- Ionian (major): 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
; plaits = 32
; tune_by_ear = on
; ionian
; 12
;  100.0   16    ; C#  (root C) -- out
;  200.0   96    ; D   (root C) -- 2nd
;  300.0   24    ; D#  (root C) -- out, the other 3rd
;  400.0  128    ; E   (root C) -- 3rd
;  500.0   64    ; F   (root C) -- 4th
;  600.0    8    ; F#  (root C) -- out, tritone
;  700.0  192    ; G   (root C) -- 5th
;  800.0   16    ; G#  (root C) -- out
;  900.0   96    ; A   (root C) -- 6th
; 1000.0   24    ; A#  (root C) -- out, the other 7th
; 1100.0  128    ; B   (root C) -- 7th
; 2/1
;
; ---- Dorian: 1 2 b3 4 5 6 b7
; plaits = 32
; tune_by_ear = on
; dorian
; 12
;  100.0   16    ; C#  (root C) -- out
;  200.0   96    ; D   (root C) -- 2nd
;  300.0  128    ; Eb  (root C) -- 3rd
;  400.0   24    ; E   (root C) -- out, the other 3rd
;  500.0   64    ; F   (root C) -- 4th
;  600.0    8    ; F#  (root C) -- out, tritone
;  700.0  192    ; G   (root C) -- 5th
;  800.0   16    ; G#  (root C) -- out
;  900.0   96    ; A   (root C) -- 6th
; 1000.0  128    ; Bb  (root C) -- 7th
; 1100.0   24    ; B   (root C) -- out, the other 7th
; 2/1
;
; ---- Phrygian: 1 b2 b3 4 5 b6 b7
; plaits = 32
; tune_by_ear = on
; phrygian
; 12
;  100.0   96    ; Db  (root C) -- 2nd
;  200.0   16    ; D   (root C) -- out
;  300.0  128    ; Eb  (root C) -- 3rd
;  400.0   24    ; E   (root C) -- out, the other 3rd
;  500.0   64    ; F   (root C) -- 4th
;  600.0    8    ; F#  (root C) -- out, tritone
;  700.0  192    ; G   (root C) -- 5th
;  800.0   96    ; Ab  (root C) -- 6th
;  900.0   16    ; A   (root C) -- out
; 1000.0  128    ; Bb  (root C) -- 7th
; 1100.0   24    ; B   (root C) -- out, the other 7th
; 2/1
;
; ---- Lydian: 1 2 3 #4 5 6 7
; plaits = 32
; tune_by_ear = on
; lydian
; 12
;  100.0   16    ; C#  (root C) -- out
;  200.0   96    ; D   (root C) -- 2nd
;  300.0   24    ; D#  (root C) -- out, the other 3rd
;  400.0  128    ; E   (root C) -- 3rd
;  500.0   16    ; F   (root C) -- out
;  600.0   64    ; F#  (root C) -- 4th (#4)
;  700.0  192    ; G   (root C) -- 5th
;  800.0   16    ; G#  (root C) -- out
;  900.0   96    ; A   (root C) -- 6th
; 1000.0   24    ; A#  (root C) -- out, the other 7th
; 1100.0  128    ; B   (root C) -- 7th
; 2/1
;
; ---- Mixolydian: 1 2 3 4 5 6 b7
; plaits = 32
; tune_by_ear = on
; mixolydian
; 12
;  100.0   16    ; C#  (root C) -- out
;  200.0   96    ; D   (root C) -- 2nd
;  300.0   24    ; D#  (root C) -- out, the other 3rd
;  400.0  128    ; E   (root C) -- 3rd
;  500.0   64    ; F   (root C) -- 4th
;  600.0    8    ; F#  (root C) -- out, tritone
;  700.0  192    ; G   (root C) -- 5th
;  800.0   16    ; G#  (root C) -- out
;  900.0   96    ; A   (root C) -- 6th
; 1000.0  128    ; Bb  (root C) -- 7th
; 1100.0   24    ; B   (root C) -- out, the other 7th
; 2/1
;
; ---- Aeolian (natural minor): 1 2 b3 4 5 b6 b7
; plaits = 32
; tune_by_ear = on
; aeolian
; 12
;  100.0   16    ; C#  (root C) -- out
;  200.0   96    ; D   (root C) -- 2nd
;  300.0  128    ; Eb  (root C) -- 3rd
;  400.0   24    ; E   (root C) -- out, the other 3rd
;  500.0   64    ; F   (root C) -- 4th
;  600.0    8    ; F#  (root C) -- out, tritone
;  700.0  192    ; G   (root C) -- 5th
;  800.0   96    ; Ab  (root C) -- 6th
;  900.0   16    ; A   (root C) -- out
; 1000.0  128    ; Bb  (root C) -- 7th
; 1100.0   24    ; B   (root C) -- out, the other 7th
; 2/1
;
; ---- Locrian: 1 b2 b3 4 b5 b6 b7
; plaits = 32
; tune_by_ear = on
; locrian
; 12
;  100.0   96    ; Db  (root C) -- 2nd
;  200.0   16    ; D   (root C) -- out
;  300.0  128    ; Eb  (root C) -- 3rd
;  400.0   24    ; E   (root C) -- out, the other 3rd
;  500.0   64    ; F   (root C) -- 4th
;  600.0  192    ; Gb  (root C) -- 5th (b5)
;  700.0   16    ; G   (root C) -- out
;  800.0   96    ; Ab  (root C) -- 6th
;  900.0   16    ; A   (root C) -- out
; 1000.0  128    ; Bb  (root C) -- 7th
; 1100.0   24    ; B   (root C) -- out, the other 7th
; 2/1
